/E (All virtual environments that have any graphics require code. A tree, a gun, and a skin we purchase on Fortnite are all defined by lines of code. For all actions, movements, and features developers write code. The more complex the game gets, the more code must be registered. As virtual worlds become more complex, more regulation will be required and the bigger the development team will become. As we look at virtual worlds like Horizon Worlds from Meta, Roblox, and Decentraland become more complex and add more features, the more complicated it will become to create these experiences. An integral part of )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
